{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception as a single automaton, with states encoding the current obstacle context. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented behavior: forward/random_walk in clear, brief direction changes to avoid obstacles, conservative recovery, and rapid return to exploration. Only one controllable is enabled per non-terminal state. All uncontrollable events are total in every state. Recovery states are one-shot and do not self-loop on controllables.",
  "strategy": [
    "Plant G1 encodes both perception and motion capability, with states for clear, obstacle-front, obstacle-left, obstacle-right, and helper commit states for action execution.",
    "Specification E1 binds each perception state to exactly one safe controllable action, prioritizing forward/random_walk in clear, rotate_clockwise for left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles, and move_backward for front obstacles, with full_rotate reserved for repeated blockages."
  ],
